# The thread dump of debug and test builds (roadmap l4.md L2), on the AT's
# Sys Req key: every thread, its state and priority, and how much of the
# kernel's one stack has been used (roadmap os-server.md P3). The keyboard
# driver asks for the dump (roadmap l4.md L8), and is running; each process
# - init's, the shell in C on the first terminal - waits for the reply of
# its thread of the OS server's, which awaits its notification (os-server.md
# P6, P12); the counter, a module (TEST_COUNTER), is ready below them. The
# mouse's driver may still be in the mouse's reset: its line is not
# checked.
program: shell
define: TEST_COUNTER
keys: {sysrq}
match: contains
---
rx286: thread root receiving priority 6
rx286: thread printer receiving priority 7
rx286: thread console receiving priority 7
rx286: thread kbd running priority 7
rx286: thread fd receiving priority 7
rx286: thread hd receiving priority 7
rx286: thread serial receiving priority 7
rx286: thread sound receiving priority 7
rx286: thread rtc receiving priority 7
rx286: thread counter ready priority 1
rx286: thread os awaiting a notification priority 5
rx286: thread thread awaiting its reply priority 3
rx286: the kernel's stack used
